WEBVTT

NOTE seasonal-profiles: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:06.010
A small set of profiles, one per
condition, is easier to run a season with.

V1a-1
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.880
Name each of the five slots
for a condition, not a date.

V1b-1
00:00:18.506 --> 00:00:20.596
A short list stays readable a year later.

V1c-1
00:00:21.706 --> 00:00:24.566
Edits to your targets leave
a saved profile out of date.

V1d-1
00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:29.306
To refresh a profile, mark its
slot under Update from Current.

V1e-1
00:00:30.406 --> 00:00:35.036
That overwrites its stored targets,
but changes no station until you apply it.

V1f-1
00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:40.040
For a one-off event, capture
into a spare slot instead.

V2a-1
00:00:45.353 --> 00:00:49.733
Applying a profile recalculates the whole
course, so treat it as a planned change.

V2b-1
00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.534
Apply it the evening before. Next morning,

V2b-2
00:00:53.634 --> 00:00:56.060
read the new suggestions
against a fresh scan.

V2c-1
00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:59.333
A profile matches stations by name.

V2c-2
00:00:59.433 --> 00:01:03.080
A renamed or renumbered station
won't match an old profile.

V2d-1
00:01:04.186 --> 00:01:06.926
Stations added after
capture keep their target.

V3a-1
00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:16.730
A profile changes targets,
and targets change deficits.

V3b-1
00:01:18.313 --> 00:01:21.963
New targets, new suggestions.
Review them before pushing.

V4-1
00:01:28.283 --> 00:01:31.963
A profile switch queues a
large push. Review it as one.
